sentences.l:
But when he had dined, and had fitted his heart with food,
and for him, having filled it, he gave the cup, from which he himself drank,
full of wine;

but at ease
drink, and other things aside let us bring to mind, and not me of these
remind;

May there be now for us two, for a time, both food
and sweet wine, to us who are inside the hut,
to feast in silence, and let others go after their work;
